Streamer: dynamicBufferDesc.size is the initial per-frame size of the dynamic buffer.

StreamerImpl::Create stores dynamicBufferDesc and never reads its size (the header says it is
ignored): the dynamic buffer starts empty, and Grow creates a committed buffer of
Align(offset, 64 KiB) * queuedFrameNum at every new per-frame high-water mark, parking the previous
one until EndFrame destroys it queuedFrameNum + 1 frames later, on the calling thread. A caller
that knows its per-frame volume pays one allocation per high-water mark, the first-touch page
faults of each fresh buffer inside the copy, and the frees inside EndStreamerFrame, for nothing.

This gives the field a meaning: a non-zero size is the initial per-frame size, allocated at
creation through Grow (rounded up to the 64 KiB chunk, times queuedFrameNum); a frame that streams
more still grows the buffer as before. 0 keeps the on-demand growth, so no existing caller changes.
Measured on v190, Vulkan and D3D12: 100 KiB with queuedFrameNum 2 gives one 262,144-byte buffer at
creation that frames streaming 64 KiB keep; a 192 KiB frame grows it to 393,216 bytes.
diff --git a/Include/Extensions/NRIStreamer.h b/Include/Extensions/NRIStreamer.h
index 0b2bab84..82f636f2 100644
--- a/Include/Extensions/NRIStreamer.h
+++ b/Include/Extensions/NRIStreamer.h
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ NriStruct(StreamerDesc) {
 
     // Dynamically (re)allocated ring-buffer for copying and rendering
     Nri(MemoryLocation) dynamicBufferMemoryLocation;                // UPLOAD or DEVICE_UPLOAD
-    Nri(BufferDesc) dynamicBufferDesc;                              // "size" is ignored
+    Nri(BufferDesc) dynamicBufferDesc;                              // "size" is the initial per-frame size (0 - allocate on demand), the buffer still grows if a frame streams more
     uint32_t queuedFrameNum;                                        // number of frames "in-flight" (usually 1-3), adds 1 under the hood for the current "not-yet-committed" frame
 
     // Statically allocated read/write ring-buffer for generic CPU data
diff --git a/Source/Shared/StreamerInterface.hpp b/Source/Shared/StreamerInterface.hpp
index 5bcf36ce..e1870157 100644
--- a/Source/Shared/StreamerInterface.hpp
+++ b/Source/Shared/StreamerInterface.hpp
@@ -59,6 +59,16 @@ Result StreamerImpl::Create(const StreamerDesc& desc) {
 
     m_Desc = desc;
 
+    // Pre-allocate the dynamic buffer if an initial per-frame size is requested (otherwise it grows on demand)
+    if (desc.dynamicBufferDesc.size) {
+        m_DynamicBufferOffset = desc.dynamicBufferDesc.size;
+
+        if (!Grow())
+            return Result::FAILURE;
+
+        m_DynamicBufferOffset = 0;
+    }
+
     return Result::SUCCESS;
 }
 
